{"record": "turn", "turn": 5, "seconds": 4.783, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 5375}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5375, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9647, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 566, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01S476w3NHXgcQyyJpA8xikD", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "The paper says hh gives a rather good fit \"so long as h is produced close to rest\", i.e. non-relativistic on-shell Higgs bosons. The conclusions add that in the mixed-channel analysis a good fit needs BR(hh) ≳ 0.8 and m_χ close to m_h.\n\nBest fit for pure hh (Tab. fitResults):\n- m_χ ≈ 125.7 (+3.1/−0) GeV\n- ⟨σv⟩ ≈ 5.33 ± 0.68 ×10⁻²⁶ cm³/s\n- χ²_min = 29.5\n- p-value = 0.13\n\nFor comparison, the b b̄ channel has m_χ ≈ 48.7 GeV, so the hh mass is more than twice as large.\n\nExplanation: the paper treats hh as a cascade annihilation, similar to hidden-sector mediator models. Each h decays mainly to b b̄, and each b quark then has energy ≈ m_h/2. The resulting b-quark spectrum is like that from b b̄ annihilation at a much lower DM mass, so the fit is good even though m_χ is over twice as heavy as in the other channels.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.1"}, {"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "6"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261117T081929Z_eval-14_staged_681c", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper says hh gives a rather good fit \"so long as h is produced close to rest\", i.e. non-relativistic on-shell Higgs bosons. The conclusions add that in the mixed-channel analysis a good fit needs BR(hh) ≳ 0.8 and m_χ close to m_h.\n\nBest fit for pure hh (Tab. fitResults):\n- m_χ ≈ 125.7 (+3.1/−0) GeV\n- ⟨σv⟩ ≈ 5.33 ± 0.68 ×10⁻²⁶ cm³/s\n- χ²_min = 29.5\n- p-value = 0.13\n\nFor comparison, the b b̄ channel has m_χ ≈ 48.7 GeV, so the hh mass is more than twice as large.\n\nExplanation: the paper treats hh as a cascade annihilation, similar to hidden-sector mediator models. Each h decays mainly to b b̄, and each b quark then has energy ≈ m_h/2. The resulting b-quark spectrum is like that from b b̄ annihilation at a much lower DM mass, so the fit is good even though m_χ is over twice as heavy as in the other channels.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.1"}, {"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "4.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1411.4647v2", "section_id": "6"}]}, "turns": 5, "seconds": 12.357, "tool_calls": 5, "tool_result_chars": 28003, "input_tokens": 12, "output_tokens": 1121, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 15022, "cache_read_input_tokens": 21885, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-17T08:19:41+00:00"}
